  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q10-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The average rate of change of $f(x)=2x^2-3x+4$ between $x=1$ and $x=k$ is 11. Find the value of $k$. Justify your answer with calculations.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=6$",
      "worked": "The endpoints must be distinct, so $k\\ne1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(1)&=2(1)^2-3(1)+4\\\\f(1)&=3\\\\\\frac{f(k)-f(1)}{k-1}&=11\\\\\\frac{2k^2-3k+1}{k-1}&=11\\\\\\frac{(2k-1)(k-1)}{k-1}&=11\\\\2k-1&=11\\\\k&=6\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: $f(6)=58$, so $\\frac{58-3}{6-1}=11$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
